glynn -- compute permanent using Glynn's formula
************************************************

  * Usage: 
        F = glynn M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a square matrix in any
        commutative ring
  * Outputs:
      * F, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the permanent of M

Description
===========

Uses Glynn's formula (see Glynn, David G. (2010), "The permanent of a square
matrix", European Journal of Combinatorics 31 (7): 1887–1891,
doi:10.1016/j.ejc.2010.01.010).

Let $M=(m_{i,j})$ be an nxn matrix. Then
$perm(M)=\sum_{\delta}\prod_{k=1}^n(\delta_k) \prod_{i=1}^n\sum_{j=1}^n
\delta_j m_{i,j}$ where the outer summation is over $\delta\in \{ -1,+1\}^n$
with $\delta_1=1$.

For example, for the 3x3 generic matrix Glynn’s formula gives $2^2 perm(M) =(a
+ b + c)(d + e + f)(g + h + i) − (a − b + c)(d − e + f)(g − h + i) −(a + b −
c)(d + e − f)(g + h − i) + (a − b − c)(d − e − f)(g − h − i)$.

Here is the permanent of a 3x3 generic matrix of variables.

+--------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[vars(0..8)]                           |
|                                                  |
|o1 = R                                            |
|                                                  |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                               |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = genericMatrix(R,a,3,3)                   |
|                                                  |
|o2 = | a d g |                                    |
|     | b e h |                                    |
|     | c f i |                                    |
|                                                  |
|             3      3                             |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                              |
+--------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : glynn M                                      |
|                                                  |
|o3 = c*e*g + b*f*g + c*d*h + a*f*h + b*d*i + a*e*i|
|                                                  |
|o3 : R                                            |
+--------------------------------------------------+

Here is the permanent of a 4x4 generic matrix of variables.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : R = QQ[vars(0..15)]                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : M = genericMatrix(R,a,4,4)                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = | a e i m |                                                             |
|     | b f j n |                                                             |
|     | c g k o |                                                             |
|     | d h l p |                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|             4      4                                                        |
|o5 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : glynn M                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = d*g*j*m + c*h*j*m + d*f*k*m + b*h*k*m + c*f*l*m + b*g*l*m + d*g*i*n +   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     c*h*i*n + d*e*k*n + a*h*k*n + c*e*l*n + a*g*l*n + d*f*i*o + b*h*i*o +   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     d*e*j*o + a*h*j*o + b*e*l*o + a*f*l*o + c*f*i*p + b*g*i*p + c*e*j*p +   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     a*g*j*p + b*e*k*p + a*f*k*p                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : R                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Here is the permanent of a 3x3 matrix of integers.

+--------------------------------------+
|i7 : M=matrix{{1,2,3},{4,5,6},{7,8,9}}|
|                                      |
|o7 = | 1 2 3 |                        |
|     | 4 5 6 |                        |
|     | 7 8 9 |                        |
|                                      |
|              3       3               |
|o7 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                |
+--------------------------------------+
|i8 : glynn M                          |
|                                      |
|o8 = 450                              |
+--------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Works in characteristic not equal to 2 because need to divide by $2^{n-1}$.
Computationally intensive for moderate size matrices.

